{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1793763256069622001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"antitoxic-malophilic-starling","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":2},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1793753553116698001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1524bd87-d873-4ec8-9102-437bb8be362f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"007c-dabe-21a5-4e92"}],"description":"docker-storage-cap.sh picks the \"modern\" builder.gc schema at BuildKit >= 0.13 and writes builder.gc.maxUsedSpace directly under gc. Two sources disagree with that:\n- BuildKit v0.17.0 release notes (PRs #5359, #5079) are where reserved and maximum storage limits first appear, so 0.13 to 0.16 builders would get a key they do not implement. That is the same silent no-op as catty-giddied-hedgehog, one version band higher.\n- The current dockerd reference example shows maxUsedSpace only INSIDE builder.gc.policy[] entries. The only space key it shows directly under gc is defaultReservedSpace, so gc-level maxUsedSpace may be ignored even on Engine 28+ (BuildKit 0.20).\nNot live on rebar-gerrit, which runs BuildKit 0.12.6 and takes the legacy defaultKeepStorage branch. Unverified: the moby daemon config struct for Engine 28 gc-level keys. Next check: read moby daemon/config BuilderGCConfig at v28.0.0, then pin the schema boundary and key placement with tests in tests/scripts/test_docker_storage_cap.py.\nFound 2026-11-03 while working alchemic-ornate-eider (session a85e3cd3).","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["ops-sweep"],"ticket_id":"5bc1-7e5b-3b4c-46c8","ticket_type":"bug","title":"docker-storage-cap modern GC schema may write an ignored key","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7cbb466f-423e-458e-8b81-04066d794ddd","1524bd87-d873-4ec8-9102-437bb8be362f"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793763256069622001,"uuid":"4536ca45-0147-46b0-8f6c-ed3a1761d6cb"}